#N canvas 30 30 1340 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 Cut It -- entry point on the Mac. Open THIS \, not main.pd \, when working off-device. The whole instrument is below: u_mother-stub draws the Organelle's front panel and impersonates mother.pd behind it. None of the panel is wired -- graph-on-parent renders iemguis and atom boxes and nothing else \, so every control binds by its send name instead. Open u_mother-stub for the plumbing \, the bench and the screen log. Everything about this module is on ref/workflow.md., f 94;
#X obj 20 140 u_mother-stub;
#X obj 20 740 u_root 17 1 /tmp 33 49 9002;
#X text 190 744 the patch itself. Everything above this line is the Mac shim \, and the device never loads any of it. The 17 is the nanoKONTROL's Pd channel and the 1 is the Launchpad's -- see below., f 60;
#X text 20 990 THESE ARE PD'S MIDI INPUT SLOTS \, not the devices' places in the system MIDI list: slot n carries channels (n-1)*16+1 upward. THEY MATCH main.pd ON PURPOSE \, which they never used to. Set the Mac's Media - MIDI Settings to the device's own order -- LAUNCHPAD FIRST \, nanoKONTROL SECOND \, in BOTH the input and the output list -- and the two entry points stop disagreeing about anything at all. ARGS 4 AND 5 ARE THE OUTPUT DEVICES \, 33 for the SP-404 and 49 for the Volca \, and they MATCH main.pd too. ⛔ TWO ARGS DIFFER \, NOT ONE. Arg 3 is /tmp because there is no /sdcard on a Mac \, and ARG 6 IS 9002 WHERE THE DEVICE USES 9001 -- u_net's inbound port. Only one process on a machine can hold a UDP port \, and this file is open in Pd while test/run.sh loads it again \, so one number for both would make every suite run print bind: Address already in use and fail the silence gate. Measured in 0.49 on macOS \, 2026-08-12. ⚠️ IT ALSO MEANS THE PHONE'S BUTTONS DRIVE THE DEVICE AND NOT THIS -- point PdParty at 9002 if you want them here., f 94;
#X text 20 1200 THE OUTPUT ORDER IS NOT OPTIONAL. m_launchpad uses its channel block as the LIGHTING channel too \, because the device's static \, flashing and pulsing modes are channels 1 \, 2 and 3 relative to its own port. That only lines up when the Launchpad's input slot and output port are the same number. Get it wrong and every static pad comes up FLASHING \, which looks like a bug in g_grid. Both m_ layers print the block they configured a couple of seconds after load -- read those before suspecting the code., f 94;
#X text 20 880 The Organelle never loads this file -- mother.pd loads main.pd by name. So u_mother-stub is never instantiated on hardware \, where its s~ and catch~ names would collide with mother's own., f 94;
